 "phase": "L14 + L15 (loading time), one gate: registered sounds loaded in place; definedness masks packed and expanded eight bytes at a time",
 "change": "L14: the catalog session's sound step loaded into a copy of the registry (var candidate = sounds), so each registration copied both dictionaries of every earlier sound; it now loads in place (the registry's load stores its entry only after its last throwing step, and any error ends the attempt, which publishes nothing). L15: OriginalStateRecord's Flat.make packs eight Bools per multiply (byte k's low bit to bit 56 + k, no carries) instead of a branch per byte, and the whole and range definedness readers expand a mask byte into eight Bools with one multiply, mask and add (byte-aligned spans; per bit at the unaligned head and the tail); a precondition checks the counts.",
 "why one gate": "L14 alone (~3% of the A12's catalog window, ~0.3 s) is below the A12's noise floor (\u00b10.6 s); the profile attributes each: catalog-window shares in the A12 L13 profile, dictionary copies of the registry ~3%, Flat.make 8.2% and per-bit definedness expansion 3.2%",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no bug; L14's three claims verified (load stores last, errors end the attempt with nothing published, no callback touches sounds during the load); both L15 formulas exact, the uninitialized-buffer contract kept, padding bits zero; follow-ups applied before the gate: tests of ranges starting mid-byte (parted records) and of the zero padding bits (extract against a fresh record), the counts precondition",
